t status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANADA, TORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIKOSHIBA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIROISHI, ISAO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEIJIN LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YATABE, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HANADA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIKOSHIBA HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIROISHI ISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YATABE TOSHIAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANADA, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIKOSHIBA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIROISHI, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YATABE, TOSHIAKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A liquid crystal device and a transparent conductive substrate preferably used as an electrode substrate constituting the liquid crystal device.  (i) The transparent conductive substrate includes a transparent polymer substrate (S), a gas-barrier layer (X), a cured resin layer (U), and a transparent conductive layer (E).  (ii) The cured resin layer (U) is in contact with the transparent conductive layer (E).  (iii) The surface of the cured resin layer (U) in contact with the transparent conductive layer (E) has a surface resistivity of more than 1.0x10&lt;13&gt;  OMEGA / in the 50  DEG C 30%RH environment, and more than 1.0x10&lt;12&gt;  OMEGA / in the 50  DEG C 90%RH environment.  The transparent conductive substrate has high gas-barrier properties and a high stability in a high-temperature high-humidity environment.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif à cristaux liquides, et un substrat conducteur transparent utilisé, de préférence, comme un substrat d'électrode constituant ledit dispositif à cristaux liquides. Dans ce dispositif, i) le substrat conducteur transparent inclut un substrat polymérique transparent (S), une couche faisant barrière aux gaz (X), une couche de résine polymérisée (U) et une couche conductrice transparente (E); ii) la couche de résine polymérisée (U) est en contact avec la couche conductrice transparente (E); iii) la surface de la couche de résine polymérisée (U) en contact avec la couche conductrice transparente (E) présente une résistivité superficielle supérieure à 1,0x10&lt;13&gt; OMEGA / dans l'environnement 50  DEG C30 %RH, et supérieure à 1,0x10&lt;12&gt; OMEGA / dans l'environnement 50 DEG C90 %RH. Le substrat conducteur transparent a des propriétés barrière aux gaz élevées et une grande stabilité dans un environnement de température élevée et de forte humidité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement 